# Internal working/planning docs — NEVER git-controlled. Put any private draft,
# strategy note, dogfood plan, or results write-up under internal/ and it is
# ignored automatically (no per-file maintenance). Polished PUBLIC docs go in
# docs/ or ROADMAP.md, not here. (The old root-level sidecar-*.md / PLAN.md were
# moved into internal/; they remain in git history — this only stops future
# tracking.)
/internal/

# Stryker mutation-testing sandboxes (transient; can be 50MB+ and are
# recreated on every run). Stryker ignores them internally, git did not —
# a `git add -A` after a run swept 1117 sandbox files into a commit.
.stryker-tmp/

# graphify's knowledge-graph output. It writes into the directory it SCANS, so
# `graphify update ./src` drops ~7MB of JSON inside src/. Same shape as the
# Stryker sandboxes above: generated, transient, and invisible to git without
# this line. Also excluded from the workspace/PKI indexers — an unexcluded
# directory of generated files inside the workspace is exactly what bloated the
# Project Knowledge Index to 330MB in v0.122.1.
graphify-out/
.graphify-venv/
/CLAUDE.md
dogfood-tmp/
# Agent-skill scaffolding: plugin-coupled label/tracker mappings.
# Durable repo conventions live in the committed AGENTS.md instead.
docs/agents/
# swebench's evaluation harness writes run logs and reports to CWD
logs/run_evaluation/
*.sidecar-*.json
